    <entry_item>
      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
      <uighur>üǰegülkü</uighur>
      <cyrillic>үзүүлэх</cyrillic>
      <transcript>YZEGYL-</transcript>
      <definition>[v. caus. of yze-] To show, demonstrate; to render service, give help; to teach; to cause, bring about, create.</definition>
      <page>1015</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠦᠨ ᠲᠠᠨᠢᠭᠤᠯᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>--yn taniγulaxu</transcript>
          <definition> To make acquainted with, familiarize with.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠮᠨᠡᠯᠭᠡ ᠎ᠶᠢᠨ ᠠᠩᠬᠠᠨ ᠤ ᠲᠤᠰᠠᠯᠠᠮᠵᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>emnelge jin angxan u tusalamzi --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To give first aid.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠰᠡᠷᠭᠦᠴᠡᠯ ᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>esergycel i --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To resist, counteract.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠰᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>esi –ky </transcript>
          <definition>To predict, prophesy</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠭᠠᠰᠢᠭᠤᠨ ᠪᠡᠷᠺᠡ ᠎ᠶᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>γasiγun berke ji --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To cause sorrow or grief</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠨᠣᠮ ᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>nom i --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To teach (especially religion);to preach.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠥᠪᠡᠷ ᠤᠨ ᠪᠡᠶ᠎ᠡ ᠎ᠪᠡᠨ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>øber yn bej-e ben --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To show one's true shape or self</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠰᠠᠭᠠᠳ ᠪᠣᠭᠤᠮᠲᠠ ᠎ᠶᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>saγad boγumta ji --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To create hindrances or obstacles; to handicap.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠰᠦᠷ ᠵᠢᠪᠬᠤᠯᠠᠩ ᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>syr zibxulang i --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To display one's strength or power, make a demonstration</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠲᠤᠰᠠᠯᠠᠮᠵᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>tusalamzi --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To give help or assistance</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠦᠯᠢᠭᠡᠷ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>yliger --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To set an example or pattern.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠵᠢᠭᠰᠠᠭᠠᠯ ᠢ ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>ziysaγal i --ky</transcript>
          <definition> To stage a demonstration.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
    <entry_item>
      <dico>Kowalewski</dico>
      <unicode>ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠺᠦ</unicode>
      <definition>montrer. faire voir. laisser voir; 2 démontrer, enseigner; 3 prouver, faire une démonstration</definition>
      <page>547</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠰᠢ ᠡᠰᠡ ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠭᠰᠡᠨ</unicode>
          <definition>qui n'est pas démontré, expliqué, prouvé; 2 arbitraire, spontané</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠺᠦ ᠬᠠᠭᠤᠳᠠᠰᠤᠨ</unicode>
          <definition>mémorial, journal</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠺᠦ ᠎ᠶᠢᠨ ᠲᠤᠯᠠ</unicode>
          <definition>pour preuve, pour convaincre, pour persuader</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠨᠣᠮ ᠢ ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠺᠦ</unicode>
          <definition>enseigner la religion</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠡᠨ ᠪᠦᠭᠡᠰᠦ ᠪᠡᠷ ᠥᠪᠡᠷ ᠤᠨ ᠪᠡᠶ᠎ᠡ ᠎ᠪᠡᠨ ᠦᠵᠡᠭᠦᠯᠦᠭᠳᠦᠨ</unicode>
          <definition>qui que tu sois, montre-toi!</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
    <entry_item>
      <dico>Schmidt</dico>
      <unicode>ᠥᠵᠠᠺᠥᠯᠺᠥ</unicode>
